MINIMUM QUALIFCIATIONS:

Graduation from an accredited college or university with a bachelor’s degree in psychology, social work, nursing, counseling, or a related field, plus 1,500 hours of clinical experience;

OR
a bachelor’s degree and a valid Qualified Mental Health Professional (QMHP) certification or Certified Substance Abuse Counselor (CSAC) certification plus 1,500 hours of clinical experience;

OR
a master’s degree in psychology, social work, nursing, counseling, or a related field plus 500 hours of clinical experience.

